(807206, 88350, 10720, '<td valign="top">I think if I had released earlier this was a water drop I would have marked it higher. I assumed it was glass that you could position the lighting just so to get this effect.  I do agree these seems as much about gold as purple but nice for either color.</td>', 'I think if I had released earlier this was a water drop I would have marked it higher. I assumed it was glass that you could position the lighting just so to get this effect.  I do agree these seems as much about gold as purple but nice for either color.', '2004-07-12 12:08:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(807213, 88342, 1368, '<td valign="top">what is the hatrick .. hmmm?</td>', 'what is the hatrick .. hmmm?', '2004-07-12 12:19:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(807219, 88133, 19035, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by flip89:</b></div><hr/><i> As a person of color, I find this a very offensive caricature. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I am not a person of color, and I too find this picture offensive.  I was the one person who reated this shot a one.</td>', 'Originally posted by flip89: As a person of color, I find this a very offensive caricature.   I am not a person of color, and I too find this picture offensive.  I was the one person who reated this shot a one.', '2004-07-12 12:25:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(807273, 88610, 19608, '<td valign="top">It''s a very colorful ornament - but the image does not really grab me.  The DoF is nice for the background - but also resulted in soft focus for area that should be sharp on the pottery and the yellow and red string / tassle.<br/> <br/>The large glare on the ornament is a detractor.</td>', 'It''s a very colorful ornament - but the image does not really grab me.  The DoF is nice for the background - but also resulted in soft focus for area that should be sharp on the pottery and the yellow and red string / tassle. The large glare on the ornament is a detractor.', '2004-07-12 13:15:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(807342, 88610, 18349, '<td valign="top">I think I would like it more without the pottery...just the purples together would be pretty.  :o)</td>', 'I think I would like it more without the pottery...just the purples together would be pretty.  :o)', '2004-07-12 13:56:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(807343, 88133, 255, '<td valign="top">ok, it took me all night, but i finally figured out what this image reminded me of. as i mentioned before, first impressions were of a weird al jolson spin, but giving the photographer the benefit of the doubt, i looked at it for quite awhile, and knew that it reminded me of something else--something about the vibrant, almost electric quality of the colors...and it finally hit me this morning. it reminds me of the old twizzler commercials, with the mouth and nothing else.</td>', 'ok, it took me all night, but i finally figured out what this image reminded me of. as i mentioned before, first impressions were of a weird al jolson spin, but giving the photographer the benefit of the doubt, i looked at it for quite awhile, and knew that it reminded me of something else--something about the vibrant, almost electric quality of the colors...and it finally hit me this morning. it reminds me of the old twizzler commercials, with the mouth and nothing else.', '2004-07-12 13:57:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(807387, 88610, 12160, '<td valign="top">This photo fits the challenge well, nice close-up and framed well. It''s tricky to photograph shiny objects but I think this was handled here well. I think you wanted the shadows to play a role in the shot b/c I think that the different shades of purple (background and table top?) are all created by light.<br/> <br/>IMO, the subject will benefit from a narrower aperture so that the  entire foreground subject is in focus. You''re probably far enough from the background to blur it. I like the decorative ball but where it''s sitting on is kind of odd. Do these two go together? It''s a nice photo nonetheless.<br/> <br/></td>', 'This photo fits the challenge well, nice close-up and framed well. It''s tricky to photograph shiny objects but I think this was handled here well. I think you wanted the shadows to play a role in the shot b/c I think that the different shades of purple (background and table top?) are all created by light. IMO, the subject will benefit from a narrower aperture so that the  entire foreground subject is in focus. You''re probably far enough from the background to blur it. I like the decorative ball but where it''s sitting on is kind of odd. Do these two go together? It''s a nice photo nonetheless. ', '2004-07-12 14:18:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(807457, 88342, 23953, '<td valign="top">How can you consider this a good picture? It isn''t a picture at all. You have altered the "picture" so much that it is no longer a picture, it is artwork. I would suggest dropping the camera and picking up a paint brush. Take your artistic talents elsewhere. You are not a photographer in my eyes!<br/> <br/>Sincerely,<br/>djtj1980</td>', 'How can you consider this a good picture? It isn''t a picture at all. You have altered the "picture" so much that it is no longer a picture, it is artwork. I would suggest dropping the camera and picking up a paint brush. Take your artistic talents elsewhere. You are not a photographer in my eyes! Sincerely,djtj1980', '2004-07-12 15:11:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(807483, 88342, 9913, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by djtj1980:</b></div><hr/><i> How can you consider this a good picture? It isn''t a picture at all. You have altered the "picture" so much that it is no longer a picture, it is artwork. I would suggest dropping the camera and picking up a paint brush. Take your artistic talents elsewhere. You are not a photographer in my eyes!<br/> <br/>Sincerely,<br/>djtj1980 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>and you are?</td>', 'Originally posted by djtj1980: How can you consider this a good picture? It isn''t a picture at all. You have altered the "picture" so much that it is no longer a picture, it is artwork. I would suggest dropping the camera and picking up a paint brush. Take your artistic talents elsewhere. You are not a photographer in my eyes! Sincerely,djtj1980   and you are?', '2004-07-12 15:24:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(807496, 88342, 23953, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nazgul:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by djtj1980:</b></div><hr/><i> How can you consider this a good picture? It isn''t a picture at all. You have altered the "picture" so much that it is no longer a picture, it is artwork. I would suggest dropping the camera and picking up a paint brush. Take your artistic talents elsewhere. You are not a photographer in my eyes!<br/> <br/>Sincerely,<br/>djtj1980 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>and you are? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Why does that matter?</td>', 'Originally posted by Nazgul: Originally posted by djtj1980: How can you consider this a good picture? It isn''t a picture at all. You have altered the "picture" so much that it is no longer a picture, it is artwork. I would suggest dropping the camera and picking up a paint brush. Take your artistic talents elsewhere. You are not a photographer in my eyes! Sincerely,djtj1980   and you are?   Why does that matter?', '2004-07-12 15:32:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(807513, 88342, 9913, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by djtj1980:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Why does that matter? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It doesnt really I was just wondering who died and made you an expert on photography c," )</td>', 'Originally posted by djtj1980: Why does that matter?   It doesnt really I was just wondering who died and made you an expert on photography c," )', '2004-07-12 15:43:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(807528, 88342, 20235, '<td valign="top">Well, I''m still failry new to the site and so this was the first time i''ve had a chance to view your work. Now I know what all the fuss is about! This photo was remarkable imho and every element in it totally worked. I voted an 8 and am glad to see it win a ribbon.... congrats! : )</td>', 'Well, I''m still failry new to the site and so this was the first time i''ve had a chance to view your work. Now I know what all the fuss is about! This photo was remarkable imho and every element in it totally worked. I voted an 8 and am glad to see it win a ribbon.... congrats! : )', '2004-07-12 15:49:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(807559, 88342, 23953, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nazgul:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by djtj1980:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Why does that matter? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It doesnt really I was just wondering who died and made you an expert on photography c," ) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I never said, nor do I claim to be an expert in photography. What I am saying is that anybody can take a bad picture and make it a good one with do time. For example, the original angel picture that this photographer took was extremely underexposed and really was a boring, non-eye catching picture. (it may have intentianal to do what was needed to be done to make it a good picture) But with time and nice photo program for your computer it can easily become a nice picture. In my mind the whole challege of photography is to capture a nice picture, not create one.</td>', 'Originally posted by Nazgul: Originally posted by djtj1980: Why does that matter?   It doesnt really I was just wondering who died and made you an expert on photography c," )   I never said, nor do I claim to be an expert in photography. What I am saying is that anybody can take a bad picture and make it a good one with do time. For example, the original angel picture that this photographer took was extremely underexposed and really was a boring, non-eye catching picture. (it may have intentianal to do what was needed to be done to make it a good picture) But with time and nice photo program for your computer it can easily become a nice picture. In my mind the whole challege of photography is to capture a nice picture, not create one.', '2004-07-12 15:58:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(807580, 88399, 9763, '<td valign="top">great, fun shot!  I love the colors and the feel.  Very crisp and great lighting &amp; composition.  great job!  The ONLY thing i might change would be to try to get the dock to be 100% flat on the horizon line (180 degrees).  Other than that, it''s great!  I didn''t vote in this challenge actually.  I wish I had.  My shot didn''t do very well, shows me for getting creative with my lighting haha!</td>', 'great, fun shot!  I love the colors and the feel.  Very crisp and great lighting & composition.  great job!  The ONLY thing i might change would be to try to get the dock to be 100% flat on the horizon line (180 degrees).  Other than that, it''s great!  I didn''t vote in this challenge actually.  I wish I had.  My shot didn''t do very well, shows me for getting creative with my lighting haha!', '2004-07-12 16:10:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(807584, 88342, 9913, '<td valign="top">ok djtj1980 show an example how you take a below average photo and turn it in to an excellent one!</td>', 'ok djtj1980 show an example how you take a below average photo and turn it in to an excellent one!', '2004-07-12 16:15:19.000000', NULL, 0),
