(807685, 88342, 21611, '<td valign="top">Wow Heida... Great shot Oh and by the way  now you know how professional athletes feel when some moron heckels them from the crowd.!!! The really good ones just go about their business as if the jerk wasnt there. <br/> <br/>And a special note to djtj. Even if thats the way you feel, why not try observing for a while and learn some things before you make a fool of yourself.</td>', 'Wow Heida... Great shot Oh and by the way  now you know how professional athletes feel when some moron heckels them from the crowd.!!! The really good ones just go about their business as if the jerk wasnt there.  And a special note to djtj. Even if thats the way you feel, why not try observing for a while and learn some things before you make a fool of yourself.', '2004-07-12 17:47:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(807718, 88342, 24100, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nazgul:</b></div><hr/><i> ok djtj1980 show an example how you take a below average photo and turn it in to an excellent one! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The picture that comes to mind is no longer available here at dpc... Only the excellent one is. I''m talking about the June free study vinner.<br/> <br/>The Silence picture is more a photo manipulation than a photo in my mind.<br/>And how can a marineblue picture win the color purple challenge?! Parts of the fabric is Purple-ish I admit. Other parts is not(in my eyes on my monitor). <br/>With this level of photo manipulation why not just shoot a grey cloth, select it and tweek it into purple?<br/> <br/>If you take this further why not take a photo, turn it into b/w, send it to a graphic artist of choice and let him/her paint it in pretty colors in Photoshop or Painter?<br/> <br/>Is this what we want? Is this really in the spirit of this photography contest?</td>', 'Originally posted by Nazgul: ok djtj1980 show an example how you take a below average photo and turn it in to an excellent one!  The picture that comes to mind is no longer available here at dpc... Only the excellent one is. I''m talking about the June free study vinner. The Silence picture is more a photo manipulation than a photo in my mind.And how can a marineblue picture win the color purple challenge?! Parts of the fabric is Purple-ish I admit. Other parts is not(in my eyes on my monitor). With this level of photo manipulation why not just shoot a grey cloth, select it and tweek it into purple? If you take this further why not take a photo, turn it into b/w, send it to a graphic artist of choice and let him/her paint it in pretty colors in Photoshop or Painter? Is this what we want? Is this really in the spirit of this photography contest?', '2004-07-12 18:31:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(807733, 88342, 14193, '<td valign="top">Heida, this picture is stunning! Two in a row, congratulations.<br/> Vision is the difference between and average photogragher (like me, below average actually) and a real artist. Keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>I had said some negative things to djtj, but edited it when I realized how new he was to the site, as my comments were about judging others when you yourself had not put your own work out to be judged. I hope that you get involved in the site and see why the site council(through much debate) decided to allow the members challenges to be post edited in this way. I think it was a good decision, as was the decision to leave the open challenge with the limited editing rules. Now we get to see the whole range of talents of the photograghers on this site, IMHO.<br/>Anyway, enjoy the site, it is really an awesome one!<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-07-12 17:51:32.</i></td>', 'Heida, this picture is stunning! Two in a row, congratulations. Vision is the difference between and average photogragher (like me, below average actually) and a real artist. Keep up the good work! I had said some negative things to djtj, but edited it when I realized how new he was to the site, as my comments were about judging others when you yourself had not put your own work out to be judged. I hope that you get involved in the site and see why the site council(through much debate) decided to allow the members challenges to be post edited in this way. I think it was a good decision, as was the decision to leave the open challenge with the limited editing rules. Now we get to see the whole range of talents of the photograghers on this site, IMHO.Anyway, enjoy the site, it is really an awesome one!', '2004-07-12 18:39:59.000000', '2004-07-12 18:51:32.000000', 0),
(807809, 88350, 19708, '<td valign="top">Hi Mark,<br/> <br/>I see the voters agreed with my vote - a well-earned 10!<br/> <br/>This is an awesome shot, and so happy it made to the top 3.</td>', 'Hi Mark, I see the voters agreed with my vote - a well-earned 10! This is an awesome shot, and so happy it made to the top 3.', '2004-07-12 19:28:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(807920, 88298, 14773, '<td valign="top">very pretty and evocative</td>', 'very pretty and evocative', '2004-07-12 20:22:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(807941, 88133, 1368, '<td valign="top">Hey congrats on your top 10 entry!<br/>I found this picture to be original and cool<br/>It reminds me a bit of the 80´s<br/>I think the composition is great and lips are perfect<br/>only thing that could have been better was maybe to have the eye a little brighter<br/>cause I see it is purple and could have worked better birghter I think<br/>Anyway I really cannot see what can be offensive about this?<br/>I think most people agree with me cause it got in the top 10 didnt it :)<br/>Keep this stuff up I can´t wait to see more of your entrys :)</td>', 'Hey congrats on your top 10 entry!I found this picture to be original and coolIt reminds me a bit of the 80´sI think the composition is great and lips are perfectonly thing that could have been better was maybe to have the eye a little brightercause I see it is purple and could have worked better birghter I thinkAnyway I really cannot see what can be offensive about this?I think most people agree with me cause it got in the top 10 didnt it :)Keep this stuff up I can´t wait to see more of your entrys :)', '2004-07-12 20:36:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(807944, 88342, 14773, '<td valign="top">It''s a very nice piece of art, but the high amount of editing makes it look more like a painting now. Still, nice work.</td>', 'It''s a very nice piece of art, but the high amount of editing makes it look more like a painting now. Still, nice work.', '2004-07-12 20:37:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(807949, 88342, 14773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nazgul:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by djtj1980:</b></div><hr/><i> How can you consider this a good picture? It isn''t a picture at all. You have altered the "picture" so much that it is no longer a picture, it is artwork. I would suggest dropping the camera and picking up a paint brush. Take your artistic talents elsewhere. You are not a photographer in my eyes!<br/> <br/>Sincerely,<br/>djtj1980 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>and you are? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is great art.  I guess we have to look at these examples like Ansel Adams landscape photos.  Those photos ARE NOT straight out of his camera, he pioneered darkroom techniques that would be the equivalent of dodging and burning. Because it''s done on a computer and not in a lab, does that make it any less legit? That''s just an example, I''m actually not on either side of the debate.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-07-12 19:40:53.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Nazgul: Originally posted by djtj1980: How can you consider this a good picture? It isn''t a picture at all. You have altered the "picture" so much that it is no longer a picture, it is artwork. I would suggest dropping the camera and picking up a paint brush. Take your artistic talents elsewhere. You are not a photographer in my eyes! Sincerely,djtj1980   and you are?   It is great art.  I guess we have to look at these examples like Ansel Adams landscape photos.  Those photos ARE NOT straight out of his camera, he pioneered darkroom techniques that would be the equivalent of dodging and burning. Because it''s done on a computer and not in a lab, does that make it any less legit? That''s just an example, I''m actually not on either side of the debate.', '2004-07-12 20:39:32.000000', '2004-07-12 20:40:53.000000', 0),
(807975, 88208, 8816, '<td valign="top">I think what this photo is missing is a clear subject - my eyes lack anything clear to be looking at.  While a convincing, interesting subject, with a little more though it could have been fantastic.<br/> <br/>Lee<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-07-14 02:44:11.</i></td>', 'I think what this photo is missing is a clear subject - my eyes lack anything clear to be looking at.  While a convincing, interesting subject, with a little more though it could have been fantastic. Lee', '2004-07-12 21:08:18.000000', '2004-07-14 03:44:11.000000', 0),
(807983, 88133, 18644, '<td valign="top">People, get a life! My wife is also of color and found this very amusing. Art, like the old Louisianna Show, old vaudeville, it''s art and it''s PURPLE!<br/> <br/>Great shot, lots of work and thought went into it. I gave this a 8 originaly, great shot!</td>', 'People, get a life! My wife is also of color and found this very amusing. Art, like the old Louisianna Show, old vaudeville, it''s art and it''s PURPLE! Great shot, lots of work and thought went into it. I gave this a 8 originaly, great shot!', '2004-07-12 21:17:24.000000', NULL, 0),
