(808050, 88133, 18517, '<td valign="top">Despite people''s closed-mindedness, this did very well and I''m thankful. Way to go!</td>', 'Despite people''s closed-mindedness, this did very well and I''m thankful. Way to go!', '2004-07-12 22:05:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(808093, 88133, 16230, '<td valign="top">Wow Kevin, you really stirred ''em up didn''t you? :) I think it''s a fantastic photo, and it really should have received the blue ribbon. If it wasn''t for a few "Oh-I-just-need-to-act-soooo-offended-so-people-will-think-I''m-a-good-person" types, then you probably would have. Way to go! True art!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wow Kevin, you really stirred ''em up didn''t you? :) I think it''s a fantastic photo, and it really should have received the blue ribbon. If it wasn''t for a few "Oh-I-just-need-to-act-soooo-offended-so-people-will-think-I''m-a-good-person" types, then you probably would have. Way to go! True art! ', '2004-07-12 22:29:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(808103, 88133, 10634, '<td valign="top">I think some people''s pants are wound a little too tight. I don''t see how this could be seen as offensive. It is very unique and creative. The detail in the face (skin texture, clarity of the eye) all add up to make this a 10 all the way. Knowing this is a self portrait makes me want to give it an 11 or 12 if that were possible.</td>', 'I think some people''s pants are wound a little too tight. I don''t see how this could be seen as offensive. It is very unique and creative. The detail in the face (skin texture, clarity of the eye) all add up to make this a 10 all the way. Knowing this is a self portrait makes me want to give it an 11 or 12 if that were possible.', '2004-07-12 22:33:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(808202, 88342, 2923, '<td valign="top">Ansel Adams dodge and burn to make teh scene more realistic. I.e. he wouldn''t dodge it until the color changse, or to create cloud effects. This is a nice photo but it is approaching digital art.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GoldBerry:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nazgul:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by djtj1980:</b></div><hr/><i> How can you consider this a good picture? It isn''t a picture at all. You have altered the "picture" so much that it is no longer a picture, it is artwork. I would suggest dropping the camera and picking up a paint brush. Take your artistic talents elsewhere. You are not a photographer in my eyes!<br/> <br/>Sincerely,<br/>djtj1980 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>and you are? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is great art.  I guess we have to look at these examples like Ansel Adams landscape photos.  Those photos ARE NOT straight out of his camera, he pioneered darkroom techniques that would be the equivalent of dodging and burning. Because it''s done on a computer and not in a lab, does that make it any less legit? That''s just an example, I''m actually not on either side of the debate. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Ansel Adams dodge and burn to make teh scene more realistic. I.e. he wouldn''t dodge it until the color changse, or to create cloud effects. This is a nice photo but it is approaching digital art. Originally posted by GoldBerry: Originally posted by Nazgul: Originally posted by djtj1980: How can you consider this a good picture? It isn''t a picture at all. You have altered the "picture" so much that it is no longer a picture, it is artwork. I would suggest dropping the camera and picking up a paint brush. Take your artistic talents elsewhere. You are not a photographer in my eyes! Sincerely,djtj1980   and you are?   It is great art.  I guess we have to look at these examples like Ansel Adams landscape photos.  Those photos ARE NOT straight out of his camera, he pioneered darkroom techniques that would be the equivalent of dodging and burning. Because it''s done on a computer and not in a lab, does that make it any less legit? That''s just an example, I''m actually not on either side of the debate. ', '2004-07-12 23:44:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(808204, 88133, 9809, '<td valign="top">Somehow I''m reminded of the Rocky Horror Picture Show! Nicely done -- and to those that found it offensive -- I think you need to revisit what is truly offensive in this world; and there is plenty to choose from. This, my friend, ain''t it though. This is just art. The black was clearly chosen to deemphasize everything but the mouth, hat, and eye (and popsicle of course) -- no other reason. <br/> <br/>That being said -- the shot is scary -- just like in the Rocky Horror Picture Show! I SEE LIPS!!!</td>', 'Somehow I''m reminded of the Rocky Horror Picture Show! Nicely done -- and to those that found it offensive -- I think you need to revisit what is truly offensive in this world; and there is plenty to choose from. This, my friend, ain''t it though. This is just art. The black was clearly chosen to deemphasize everything but the mouth, hat, and eye (and popsicle of course) -- no other reason.  That being said -- the shot is scary -- just like in the Rocky Horror Picture Show! I SEE LIPS!!!', '2004-07-12 23:46:17.000000', NULL, 0),
