(825390, 87668, 13610, '<td valign="top">I like the flower, the composition is good too. More DOF would have helped your photo in my taste and a little bit more contrast. You seem to have picked the perfect time to shoot this flower. More saturation would have given more punch to your purple. Lot of details for a flower that seem so small.</td>', 'I like the flower, the composition is good too. More DOF would have helped your photo in my taste and a little bit more contrast. You seem to have picked the perfect time to shoot this flower. More saturation would have given more punch to your purple. Lot of details for a flower that seem so small.', '2004-07-26 01:27:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(837144, 88333, 16188, '<td valign="top">I love this shot - so great are the angle of view and the clarity that I feel I am in another world.  It''s also like I''m looking at lily pads instead of hydrangea.  Beautifully shot and conceived.</td>', 'I love this shot - so great are the angle of view and the clarity that I feel I am in another world.  It''s also like I''m looking at lily pads instead of hydrangea.  Beautifully shot and conceived.', '2004-08-02 13:05:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(846244, 88436, 12611, '<td valign="top">This is a fantastic composition, most notably because of the expression it seems. I don''t agree with much of the criticism because lately the most im[portant aspect of photography for me is emotion and where the eye is "forced" to go in the shot. Here, the eye is wants to look at the gloss off the hair or the shine of teh lips, but instead is forced to the area directly below the eye, peripherally viewing th erest of the photo. That gives the photo its charm and enhances the composition.<br/> <br/>There is one criticism, I have viewd several of your shots and it could be my monitor or yours but the deep richness appears to be lacking, on this shot. The contrast? levels, I don''t know- but if you use the rule that the focal point of the conposition is the area where darkest meets lightest- your darks in this photo could be a bit darker, and it would really be killer.<br/> <br/>anyway- its just my unlearned opinion- great shot.</td>', 'This is a fantastic composition, most notably because of the expression it seems. I don''t agree with much of the criticism because lately the most im[portant aspect of photography for me is emotion and where the eye is "forced" to go in the shot. Here, the eye is wants to look at the gloss off the hair or the shine of teh lips, but instead is forced to the area directly below the eye, peripherally viewing th erest of the photo. That gives the photo its charm and enhances the composition. There is one criticism, I have viewd several of your shots and it could be my monitor or yours but the deep richness appears to be lacking, on this shot. The contrast? levels, I don''t know- but if you use the rule that the focal point of the conposition is the area where darkest meets lightest- your darks in this photo could be a bit darker, and it would really be killer. anyway- its just my unlearned opinion- great shot.', '2004-08-06 08:44:19.000000', NULL, 0),
